
## Elixir-Specific

### Architecture
- **Framework:** {{ELIXIR_FRAMEWORK}} <!-- Phoenix / bare Elixir -->
- **Frontend:** {{ELIXIR_FRONTEND}} <!-- LiveView / API-only / SPA -->
- **OTP patterns:** GenServer, Supervisor trees as needed

### Key Paths

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `lib/<app>/` | Business logic (contexts) |
| `lib/<app>_web/` | Web layer (controllers, views, LiveViews) |
| `lib/<app>_web/live/` | LiveView modules |
| `lib/<app>/application.ex` | Supervision tree |
| `priv/repo/migrations/` | Ecto migrations |
| `test/` | ExUnit tests |
| `config/` | Environment configs |

### Testing
- **Framework:** ExUnit
- **Run all:** `mix test`
- **Run specific:** `mix test <path>`
- **Run with coverage:** `mix test --cover`
- **Watch mode:** `mix test.watch` (if dep installed)

### Style
- **Formatter:** `mix format`
- **Linter:** `mix credo` (if installed)
- **Dialyzer:** `mix dialyzer` (if installed)

### Elixir Conventions
- **Contexts:** Group related functions in context modules (not in schemas)
- **Schemas:** Keep schemas lean — validations and changesets only
- **Pattern matching:** Prefer pattern matching over conditionals
- **Pipe operator:** Use `|>` for data transformation chains
- **with statements:** Use `with` for multi-step operations that can fail
- **GenServer:** Only when you need state or message passing — don't overuse
- **Error tuples:** Return `{:ok, result}` / `{:error, reason}` — let callers decide how to handle

### Database
- **ORM:** Ecto
- **Migrate:** `mix ecto.migrate`
- **Rollback:** `mix ecto.rollback`
- **Seed:** `mix run priv/repo/seeds.exs`
